<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-FRENCH SOLO TOPPLES CIPOLLINI.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-FRENCH SOLO TOPPLES CIPOLLINI.</headline>
<dateline>LA CHATRE, France 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frenchman Alain Vasseur broke previous leader Mario Cipollini's grip on the Tour de France with a solo victory over 147 kms on Thursday.</p>
<p>He finished 2:32 clear of Australian teammate Stuart O'Grady and third-placed Italian Marco Artunghi after the 261.5 kms fifth leg from Chantonnay.</p>
<p>Vasseur takes over the yellow jersey of Tour leader with an advantage of 2:17 over Cipollini with German Erik Zabel, 2:19 in arrears.</p>
<p>Britain's Chris Boardman who held the lead for a day is fourth, 2:54 behind teammate Vasseur who at one point led the race by 17:45.</p>
</text>
